==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Kitaro Cat & Nezumi-Otoko Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Similarly to [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]], Kitaro Cat & Nezumi-Otoko Cat are used as a short-range tank to deal quick and high wave damage.

Despite having lower health, speed and slightly lower DPS than Cats in the Cradle, Kitaro Cat has a lower cost, faster attack rate and [[Wave Attack]]s in all forms rather than just in [[True Form]], making him slightly better in some situations, especially early on or against [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Zombies]].

Kitaro Cat excels in stages where they can get a clean hit off due to it featuring enemies with LDs or low attack frequencies. Enemies such as [[Dolphina]], and [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] are good examples of this. Enemies with Omni Strike are also vulnerable, as they tend to move closer than they should be, hence causing them to take damage from the wave attack.

Their high stats and massive level 3 Wave Attack allow them to hit every Zombie on the field, potentially even [[Zombie Killer|Z-killing]] them if you're lucky enough. This means they're much better at cleaning Zombie peons than even the original Cats in the Cradle, but their wave level and quicker time between attacks makes them a better choice for non-Zombie peons too.

